 * Output-parameters are only applied if the current code-block exits its
   branch at the 'proper' point.

 * GASP preparsing code does not track the current filename.

 * ps2gl GL_QUADS renderers do not render (filed 2026-05-11):
   ps2gl's quad-specialised shaders (general_quad, general_pv_diff_quad,
   general_nospec_quad) produce VSM output that renders nothing on PCSX2.
   The triangle siblings (general, general_pv_diff, general_nospec) work.
   Building ps2gl with -DPS2GL_USE_SCE_VSM=ON (bypasses openvcl, uses the
   Sony reference VSMs) makes the same shaders render correctly, so the
   fault is in openvcl's emitted code, not in ps2gl host-side code.
   First lead: VI02 (the xtop output / GIF DMA base address) appears to
   be reused as a loop scratch in the openvcl-emitted quad shaders, e.g.
   in build-test/vu1/general_quad_vcl.vsm near lines 28-31:
       iadd VI02, VI03, VI09
       iadd VI05, VI02, VI09
       iadd VI02, VI05, VI09
   The triangle version uses VI05/VI06 instead.  Reproducible on the
   baseline ps2gl-branch commit e407703 -- predates the recent
   (bc41a56/303c528/41dff12/5c0227b/a2a7d9d) work.

   Workaround: -DPS2GL_USE_SCE_VSM=ON.
   Investigation continues; see test/integration if a small repro
   shader can be extracted.

   ---------- Fixed entries kept for reference ----------

 * (FIXED) The 'range' modifier for .init_vf / .init_vi now works
   end-to-end: extractRegister parses "vfXX-vfYY" / "viXX-viYY" into
   a Content::RANGE argument and the Tokenizer expands the range
   into the same availableFloats / availableIntegers bits the
   comma-list form sets.  Inverted ranges (lower > upper) are
   rejected.  Regression-pinned by
   test/integration/test_init_vf_range.cpp.

 * (FIXED) CLIP operand validation: the parser was already emitting
   "Invalid argument" diagnostics for malformed CLIP operands, but
   Error::Display did not bump any counter, so main() exited 0 even
   when errors had been reported.  Error::HasErrors now tracks
   non-warning errors and the main loop uses it to fail the build.
   Regression-pinned by test/integration/test_clip_validation.cpp.

 * (FIXED) The register-allocator used to be strictly line-based and miss
   reuse of values across loop iterations (e.g. 'move test,test' with no
   subsequent dependency).  Loop back-edges now extend the live range of
   pre-loop aliases through the loop body (commit 303c528).

 * (FIXED) The expression evaluator used to output a float where a hex
   value was required for LOI immediates.  The 'raw' modifier and the
   matching IEEE-754 hex emission path were added in commit bc41a56.
